{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And Israel bowed.</b> תַּעֲלָא בְּעִידָּנֵיהּ סְגִיד לֵיהּ — He prostrated at his time [of death]." "<b>At the head of the bed.</b> He turned himself toward the Shekhinah. From here the Sages said that the Shekhinah is above the head of a sick person (Shabbat 12, Nedarim 40); another interpretation of ״עַל רֹאשׁ הַמִּטָּה״ — that his bed was whole and there was no wrongdoing in it, for Yosef is a king, and moreover he was taken captive among the nations, and behold he stands in his righteousness."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {0 "Rashi cites a targumic Aramaic phrase: 'He gave thanks at his time' or 'He prostrated at his appointed time.'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:03:54.300152091Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}